flowchart LR
    accTitle: From source drift to a trusted release
    accDescr: Complete governance flow. Register approved sources, perform scheduled detection and review, map impact, propose evidence-linked updates, run checks, require human approval of an exact revision, publish a versioned release, monitor it, and retain bounded rollback evidence. A supplied observation dated 2026-09-20 reports scheduled corpus inspection but does not establish automatic provider-source comparison or end-to-end publication.

    S[(Approved source registry)] --> D[Scheduled detection and review]
    D --> I[Map affected claims, lessons, assessments, and checks]
    I --> P[Draft evidence-linked proposal]
    P --> E{Factuality, citation, consistency, and assessment checks pass?}
    E -->|Fail and correct proposal| P
    E -->|Pass to human preview| H{Human preview and approval}
    H -->|Revise and return proposal| P
    H -->|Approve exact revision| R[Versioned release and audit record]
    R --> M[Monitor quality and freshness]
    M -->|Healthy and routine review| S
    M -->|Regression and rollback| B[Rollback with recorded reason]
    B -->|Restored scope and retained incident| S
